    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i checked the amount and currency and they look right. i did see that the error response body has a 'decline_code' field but it's being weirdly vague. is there a specific way to log the full response so i can see exactly what's happening during the handshake? also, could these types of errors be caused by something 'hiding' in the request or just some random glitch in the API?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Logging the full response is crucial; you need to capture the entire JSON payload returned by Stripe to see the granular details. Most programming languages have built-in HTTP client libraries that allow you to log the raw response object before you parse it. If you're using a library, ensure you're logging the *entire* response body, not just the error message you're currently catching. Sometimes, these vague errors are caused by subtle data mismatches, like an incorrect customer ID or an expired token, which are much more specific than a general \"decline code.\"",
      "source": "target",
